# Review: Implement slugify

## Blocking finding

**B1 — `src/slugify.mjs` is missing the required project-convention header line.**
The project checklist requires every module under `src/` to begin with the exact line:

    // woof-acceptance: 8b605207dc64

`src/slugify.mjs` line 1 is `export function slugify(text) {`. The required line is absent, and nothing else in the repo contains `woof-acceptance`. `src/slugify.mjs` is the only module under `src/`. Fix: insert `// woof-acceptance: 8b605207dc64` as the very first line of `src/slugify.mjs`, before the `export`.

## Acceptance criteria (verified by reading the code and running `node --test`)

- Lowercases input: holds. `text.toLowerCase()`; the "lowercases text" test passes.
- Runs of chars other than a–z/0–9 become one hyphen: holds. `.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-")`, applied after lowercasing; the "one -- two___three...4" test passes.
- No leading/trailing hyphens: holds. `.replace(/^-|-$/g, "")` strips at most one hyphen per end, which is enough because the previous step already collapsed runs. The boundary-trim test passes.
- Tests pass with `node --test`: holds. 4/4 pass, 0 fail. Tests are in `test/slugify.test.mjs` and use `node:test`.

## Other notes (non-blocking)

- Completion report claims match the repo state. It does not mention the header requirement, which is the gap.
- Only `src/slugify.mjs` (modified) and `test/slugify.test.mjs` (new) changed. The tests are not under `src/`, so the header convention does not apply to them.
- Non-string input throws (`text.toLowerCase` on a non-string). The task does not specify this, so it is not raised as a finding.

## Verdict

Fail, on B1 only. The implementation and tests are otherwise correct.

